TEXT 0 -480 Left 2 ;Lecture 10 (26-Oct-2026), slides 4-6: plane-wave transmission through drywall 1 cm | insulation 3 cm | brick 5 cm | air 1 cm | wood 2 cm
TEXT 0 -448 Left 2 ;Per unit area, impedance analogy: V = pressure [Pa], I = particle velocity [m/s]. Solids = series mass rho*l, soft layers = shunt compliance l/(rho c^2) or a lossless line.
TEXT 0 -400 Left 2 !.param r1=600 c1=6000 l1=0.01 r2=200 c2=500 l2=0.03 r3=2000 c3=3600 l3=0.05 r4=1.2 c4=343 l4=0.01 r5=550 c5=4000 l5=0.02 r0=1.2 c0=343.0
